-- title:
--   Ideal-theoretic and idelic norm indices agree
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra, and let $\mathfrak f$ be a nonzero ideal of $\mathcal O_K$. Let $\mathrm{Nrm}$ be a group homomorphism from the idele units $(\mathbb A_L)^\times$ to $(\mathbb A_K)^\times$ subject to three conditions. First, [`HeckeCharacter.IsAdjuster`](def/LanglandsTunnell_ArtinCoreCTM.html#L246) is preserved: whenever $u \in (\mathbb A_L)^\times$ and $\alpha \in L^\times$ satisfy, at the extended modulus $\mathfrak f \mathcal O_L$, that the finite component of $u\alpha^{-1}$ has valuation $1$ at every prime dividing the modulus and differs from $1$ there by valuation at most $\exp(-e)$ with $e$ the exact exponent of that prime in the modulus, and that $u\alpha^{-1}$ has positive real projection at every embedding $L \to \mathbb R$, then $\mathrm{Nrm}(u)$ and $\mathrm{N}_{L/K}(\alpha)$ satisfy the same conditions at $\mathfrak f$ over $K$. Second, the fractional-ideal content of $\mathrm{Nrm}(u)$ (via `projFin` then `fadContentHom`, i.e. $\prod_v \mathfrak p_v^{-\log \mathrm{v}(u_v)}$) equals `fracRelNormUnit`, the relative-norm map $\prod_w \mathfrak p_{w \cap K}^{f(w)\,\mathrm{ord}_w}$, applied to the content of $u$. Third, `unitIdeles K 𝔣` — the ideles that are units at all finite primes, congruent to $1$ modulo $\mathfrak f$ in the above sense, and positive at every real embedding — lies in the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$. Then the index, inside the group of fractional-ideal units of $K$ coprime to $\mathfrak f$ (those with zero count at each prime dividing $\mathfrak f$), of the subgroup generated by `narrowRaySubgroup K 𝔣` together with the relative norms of fractional ideals of $L$ coprime to $\mathfrak f \mathcal O_L$, equals the index in $(\mathbb A_K)^\times$ of the subgroup generated by the principal ideles and the range of $\mathrm{Nrm}$.
--
--   This is the classical comparison of the ideal-theoretic and idelic formulations of the norm index: the content map, after adjusting an idele by a principal idele so that it becomes a unit congruent to $1$ at the primes dividing $\mathfrak f$ and positive at the real places, identifies the two quotients. It is used to transfer first- and second-inequality index bounds between the two settings, and is cited in the construction of the Artin symbol for admissible moduli and in the divisibility of the index of a norm coset for extensions of prime degree.
